PROJECT: FINANCIAL TRANSACTION PLATFORM

BUSINESS PROBLEM

A fintech startup wants to build a system for managing customers' financial accounts and transactions.

The system must manage:

Customers
Financial accounts
Transactions
Recipients
Merchants
Spending categories
REQUIREMENTS

2.1 CUSTOMER

Each customer has:

CustomerID
Name
Email
Phone
Date of Birth

A customer can own multiple accounts.

Each account belongs to exactly one customer.

Customer email must be unique.

2.2 ACCOUNT

Each account has:

AccountID
Account Number
Account Type
Current Balance
Status
Created Date

Account types can be:

CHECKING
SAVINGS
WALLET

An account can perform many transactions.

Account number must be unique.

Account balance cannot be negative if the account does not allow overdraft.

2.3 TRANSACTION

Each transaction has:

TransactionID
Transaction Date/Time
Amount
Transaction Type
Status
Description

Transaction types can be:

DEPOSIT
WITHDRAWAL
TRANSFER
PAYMENT

Business rules:

Each transaction must be associated with one account that sends or spends the money.
A transfer can be associated with one receiving account.
An account can appear in many transactions.
Transaction amount must be greater than 0.
Every transaction must have a status.

2.4 MERCHANT

The system stores merchant information:

MerchantID
Name
Business Type

Business rules:

A merchant can have many payment transactions.
A payment transaction can be associated with zero or one merchant.
Deposits, withdrawals, and transfers do not necessarily have a merchant.

2.5 CATEGORY

Transactions can be classified into categories such as:

Food
Transport
Shopping
Entertainment
Bills
Other

Business rules:

A category can contain many transactions.
A transaction can belong to zero or one category.

2.6 RECIPIENT

Customers can save recipients for faster money transfers.

Business rules:

A customer can save multiple recipients.
A recipient can be saved by multiple customers.
Therefore, the relationship between Customer and Recipient is many-to-many.
This many-to-many relationship must be resolved when converting the ER model into a relational model.

2.7 TRANSACTION HISTORY

The system must maintain transaction history.
A transaction must not be deleted simply because an account is closed.
A transaction must retain its timestamp and status.
FINANCIAL INTEGRITY RULES

The system must ensure:

Account balance cannot be negative if the account does not allow overdraft.
Transaction amount must be greater than 0.
Account number must be unique.
Customer email must be unique.
Every transaction must have a status.
